    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῡσί̆-ζωνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		of a soldier, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unequipped,
				ungirded, unarmed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				8.24.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>loosing the zone</i>, i.e. ceasing to be a maid, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>: hence as epith. of Eileithyia and Artemis, who <i>assisted
				women in travail</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				36.5
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
